messages:
maya: Heads up — since ~03:02 UTC we're seeing a regional pulse of 429s from the us-west GPU pools (admission queue jump). dashboard: https://console.redwood.ai/pools/us-west/metrics -> admission_queue = 1.2k :grimacing:
opsbot: ALERT @eng-infra — pool us-west-3 admission_fill 78% -> saturation warning. top callers: embedder-service, chat-proxy.
sam: do we have sample request headers from affected clients? are they getting Retry-After or any custom header?
lee: just pulled a few logs — most responses are plain `HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests` with no Retry-After, but ~30% include `X-Admission-Hint` with short key-value string.
jordan: example we logged: `HTTP/1.1 429`
  `X-Admission-Hint: capacity=constrained;queue=high;recommended_retry=1`
  sometimes `Retry-After: 2` if the admission controller set it explicitly.
zara: hmm. SDKs assume Retry-After only. if they get 429 with no Retry-After they do exponential backoff w/ base 500ms — that's why some clients hammer after 1s. we should standardize semantics. :thinking: 
sam: agree. proposal: add a deterministic header `X-Admission-Pulse: mode=soft-queue;target-latency=150ms;retry_s=1` and document precedence: `X-Admission-*` > `Retry-After` > client default. thoughts?
maya: +1 for precedence rule. For immediate mitigation can we flip a short-term admission-policy to emit `Retry-After` for older clients?
jordan: yes — we can enable `emit_retry_after_for_legacy=true` on the admission layer per pool. rollout is trivial. ops, can we toggle on us-west-3?
opsbot: ACTION CREATED #OP-4392 — emit_retry_after_for_legacy enabled on us-west-3 target. change queued for 03:30 UTC.
lee: SDK change notes (short):
```js
// pseudo parsing logic
if (res.status === 429) {
  const hint = res.headers['x-admission-hint'] || res.headers['x-admission-pulse'];
  if (hint) {
    // parse key=val; pairs, prefer recommended_retry or retry_s
    const r = parseHint(hint).recommended_retry || parseHint(hint).retry_s;
    backoff = r ? r * 1000 : defaultBackoff();
  } else if (res.headers['retry-after']) {
    backoff = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after'], 10) * 1000;
  } else {
    backoff = jitteredExponential();
  }
}
```
zara: also recommend adding a short client-side local admission queue: allow N inflight per user key and refuse locally if exceeded (fast-fail) — that reduces thundering herd to servers. put default N=4 for text-generation calls.
sam: can we add telemetry to SDKs to surface which header clients saw (none | retry-after | admission-hint) so we can measure adoption?
jordan: yes — will add `client.admission.header_seen` metric with tag values. rollout in next SDK patch.
maya: thanks — enabling legacy Retry-After should reduce immediate errors. follow-ups: document header format in /docs/clients/admission.md and coordinate SDK patch release. I'll own the docs. :thumbsup:
zara: filing a tiny RFC to standardize grammar for `X-Admission-Hint` (kv pairs; numeric seconds). will link to the RFC in this thread when done.
opsbot: NOTE: mitigation toggle applied (emit_retry_after_for_legacy=true) at 03:30 UTC for us-west-3. monitor for 30m.
sam: great. if after 30m the tail 95 latency still spikes let's schedule a short capacity bump for us-west-3. for now, SDK changes + legacy header should smooth clients.
maya: closing loop here once metrics look sane in 1h. thanks folks.
